  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The average kinetic energy of a molecule of the gas &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>.</p><p>Average kinetic energy&nbsp;of one molecule of gas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;Boltzmann&nbsp;constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is absolute temperature.</p><p>So, from above relation we can say average kinetic energy of molecule is directly proportional to absolute temperature.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
